<title>TAIWAN: China Steel plans T$1.5/share dividend.</title>
<headline>China Steel plans T$1.5/share dividend.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-09-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's China Steel Corp said on Saturday it planned to issue a dividend of T$1.50 per share for 1995/96 (July/June) for its common share and preferred share.</p>
<p>The firm's board meeting on Saturday passed the proposals, which still need approval by its shareholders' meeting scheduled to be held on November 6, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>But the statement did not point out whether the dividend would be a cash or a stock dividend, or bonus issue.</p>
<p>China Steel, the island's largest steel maker, was privatised in April 1995.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (5080815)</p>
